    "body": "Well, that might be a better question for a place like StackOverflow. But here's some quick code I can think of:\n\n``` js\nfor (const element of document.querySelectorAll(\"*\")) {\n  for (const attribute in element.attributes) {\n    if (isBooleanAttribute(element.localName, attribute) {\n      const value = element.getAttribute(attribute);\n      if (value !== \"\" && value !== attribute) {\n        throw new Error(`Element ${element}'s boolean attribute ${attribute} is an invalid value`);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nHere `isBooleanAttribute(elementLocalName, attributeName)` is a function you'd have to implement yourself, using the table of attributes in the spec.\n\nI'm going to close this, since it seems like it's not an issue with the HTML Standard. If you have further questions, you can feel free to continue asking in the closed thread, but you might get more response from a place like StackOverflow that is focused on solving programming problems, instead of this repository, which is intended to improve the HTML Standard.\n",
